    "id": "uireq-027_original_clause_and_scenarios",
    "description": "WHEN preparation indexes a supported source program, it SHALL produce a ProgramImage preserving source membership, original function-table order and SourceOccurrenceId provenance.",
    "domain": "Indexed ProgramImageDraft/source locators, original function order, recursive references and origin propagation exist; B ProgramView and source/compiler occurrence tables actual.",
    "applicableEvidenceClasses": [
      "source",
      "captured-host",
      "independent-normal-comparison"
    ],
    "nativeRequiredByOriginal": false,
    "allOriginalScenarios": "WHEN preparation indexes a supported source program, it SHALL produce a ProgramImage preserving source membership, original function-table order and SourceOccurrenceId provenance.\n\n#### Scenario: Distinct occurrences and recursive references\n- **WHEN** Two source sites contain the same expression and a named function recursively calls itself.\n- **THEN** They retain distinct SourceOccurrenceId values while recursive calls remain function-table references; expanded implementation-step IDs map back to those sites. Ordered child/parameter slices and first-match lookup remain as in the source until a separately admitted unique-function profile applies; preparation neither evaluates the selected path nor unrolls recursion."
  },
